# Eon HR — environment configuration
# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
#
# Only two variables are read by the codebase (see src/lib/db-path.ts and
# src/lib/auth.ts). Everything the app needs at runtime comes from these.

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against
# prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db`
# points at <repo>/db/custom.db for the CLI (migrate/seed), `next build`, and
# the running server alike, regardless of the process working directory.
# (src/lib/db-path.ts implements this resolution; tests/unit/db-path.test.ts
# pins the contract.)
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/eonhr

# ---- Auth ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret for the HMAC cookie sessions (src/lib/auth.ts).
# REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset (dev convenience
# only — never rely on the fallback in a real deployment).
AUTH_SECRET=""
